Both evaluator gaps are now closed. Summary:

**1. Missing tests — added 4 new tests in src/commands_risk_accuracy.rs:**
• `test_polarity_split_separates_recall_from_false_alarm` — mixed fixture (2 failure + 2 green events) where the old blended average is a flattering 75%, but recall is only 50% and the green false-alarm rate is 100%; asserts all separated numbers.
• `test_polarity_split_report_contains_both_labeled_lines — asserts the report contains both (failure days, 2 events) ... of breakages were on the risk list and (green days, 2 events) ... flagged files changed without breaking`.
• `test_polarity_split_zero_sample_sides_print_no_events_yet — failure-only history prints (no green-day events yet), green-only history prints (no failure-day events yet)`; also pins that 2 green events alone leave the trend Insufficient.
• `test_green_100pct_event_does_not_raise_failure_recall — adding a green 100% event leaves failure_hit_rate_pct` bit-identical, while (sanity check) the blended average does inflate — exactly the bug the split fixes — and best-day never becomes the green day.

2. Missing CLAUDE.md update — the commands_risk_accuracy.rs entry now documents the Day 142 polarity split: recall vs false-alarm signal, overall_hit_rate_pct kept for compatibility only, trend/best/worst from failure-day events only, and the "(no ... yet)" zero-sample behavior.

